Ahoy.

I've been trying to pull this off for a while - ascend a dwarf, elf or
orc wearing using the appropriate racial armour and weapons.

Dwarves can get AC -27 before protection from a full set of +5 gear
(counting iron boots as dwarvish - that's a little arbitrary, I admit)
but will probably be happier with -20, no roundshield, and a dwarvish
mattock, which damage-wise is comparable to a good artifact.

Elves can get AC -35 since their armour isn't as good as dwarvish
stuff, but can be enchanted to +7. Their best single weapon is, er,
Orcrist.

(You might have a case for calling Mjollnir dwarvish and Stormbringer
elven, but I don't really see it that way.)

Orcs can get -16 (I think - IDHTSIFOM - it's something like that
anyway) which doesn't sound so bad if you add another 9 or so points
of protection, but their weapons suck; the best they can do seems to
be to two-weapon Grimtooth and an orcish short sword, and that means
no shield.

If you want to try and ascend a naked gnome with an aklys, go ahead.

Dwarves already look easiest, and they are, partly because dwarvish
gear is easiest to find in the early game if you do the Mines first,
but mainly because of the biggest problem with racial gear
ascensions...

...which is getting magic resistance. The way it works out, you have
to either play a wizard in what's not going to be a particularly
good-for-spellcasting game, or convert after your own Quest and wish
for another class's quest artifact - or play a dwarf. Or ascend
MR-less.

If you want two MR artifacts just in case - and I do, because on my
first try my dwarvish caveman got double-troubled by Rodney, the
Sceptre of Might stolen, and touch-of-deathed by a summoned master
lich - you have to play a dwarf or convert.

After that one encouraging try my dwarvish cavemen and archeologists
kept dying, mainly because they're not tough enough classes to survive
naked and weaponlsess for the early game. So I figured I may as well
wish for both MR sources, and fired up a dwarvish Valk.

And got lucky.

I played the game on my other machine, which is incommunicado at the
moment, so I don't have a big character dump, but here's what I
remember:

- ascended with full +5 armour and protection, taking me to AC -31,
and a +7 mattock. I learned the hard way that you should keep at least
one potion of holy water (or scroll of remove curse) in your main
inventory if you're going to fight major liches with a two-handed
weapon.

- got the amulet of reflection from Sokoban, which is just as well
since I didn't feel like storming the castle, or doing the quest,
without reflection, and I wasn't getting MR before the castle unless I
got *really* lucky.

- got the Master Key of Thievery and the Orb of Detection for my first
two wishes, no problem. As it happened the Key never got stolen, so
the Orb stayed in my bag. It's like guaranteeing yourself a sunny day
by remembering your umbrella.

- nastiest bit: master lich (or something) gates in Yeenoghu, Yeenoghu
gates in Demogorgon. No stoning in this game. It wouldn't have been
*so* bad if Yeenoghu hadn't had a wand of digging; Demo kept following
him down the holes. I crossed about six levels before I killed them
off.

- mattock makes digging out Gehennom easy. I even engraved directions
on all the down stairs, which was helpful since there were so many
mind flayers this game.

- first time lucky on the Astral Plane. I only had to fight Famine.

- that's all I can remember.

